    "subtitles": {
        "en": "WEBVTT\n\nNOTE Lecture 3, transcribed by hand\n\n1\n00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.000\nWelcome to the third lecture on cell biology.\n\n2\n00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.500\nToday we look at membranes &amp; transport.\n\n3\n00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:07.000\n<v Ada>Every cell is enclosed by a membrane.</v>\n\n4\n00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:15.000\nThe membrane is a double layer\nof lipids.\n\n5\n00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:18.000\nSmall molecules pass the membrane by diffusion.\n\n6\n00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:08.000\nWater moves by Osmosis, towards the higher concentration of solutes.\n\n7\n00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:06.000\nLarger molecules need transport proteins.\n\n8\n00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:14.000\nActive transport uses energy to move molecules against the gradient.\n\n9\n00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:40.000\nTo sum up: diffusion, osmosis and active transport.\n"
    }
